// REQUIRES: host-linux-amd64 || host-linux-arm64
// RUN: %python %S/Inputs/run-panics.py %S/Inputs/panics --names div-int,shift-left,index-array,index-after-output,assign-order-call,assign-order-tuple -- %gopp build %gopp_link_flags
// P04.04 (D4.12, ADR-0028 rule 3.3): a failed check ends the program with
// exit status 2 and Go's first line on standard error ("panic: runtime
// error: ..."), after the output that came before. Division and shift
// checks (a smoke of six programs) here, index checks in core-panics-index.long.test, every program of
// Inputs/panics in core-panics.long.test, and on arm64 in
// core-panics-arm64.test and core-panics-arm64.long.test.
// Inputs/panics/*.gopp are Go programs: .out and .err are `go run`'s
// (the output before the panic, and its first line), made by
// Inputs/gen-panics.py and Inputs/gen-goldens.py.
